  "body": "### Summary\n\n`GlassLeftoversTests` (#1141) samples the smiley search switch at `x = 0.95W`, which falls on the white knob on an iPad (always red in light there) and depends on the « Tous les mots clés » setting stored in the test host's defaults. CI runs on an iPhone, so nothing fails today; make the test device- and state-independent. (Opus round 3 review of #1141, Lows 1–2.)\n\n### Scope\n\n- `App/SwiftHFRTests/Common/GlassLeftoversTests.swift:185`: sample the switch track at `bar.maxX - 20` (or from the switch's own frame) instead of `0.95W`.\n- Reset `AnswerView.smileys.search.allKeywords` in `smileySheet` before the case (and restore after).\n- Keep the `.opacity(0)` mutation log this time.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The suite green on iPhone 18 Pro, iPhone SE and iPad Pro 13 simulators, light and dark, with the setting on and off; red under the `.opacity(0)` and `.background(.bar)` mutations.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
